‘\`’
     Matches only at the start of pattern space.  This is different from
     ‘^’ in multi-line mode.

     Compare the following two examples:

          $ printf "a\nb\nc\n" | sed 'N;N;s/^/X/gm'
          Xa
          Xb
          Xc

          $ printf "a\nb\nc\n" | sed 'N;N;s/\`/X/gm'
          Xa
          b
          c

‘\'’


